# Secrets -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Real environment files never enter git; the committed .env.example templates
# are what a new machine builds them from (scripts/make-env.sh).
.env
.secrets.env
stacks/*/.env

# This machine's standing answers for the handful of gateway settings it is
# allowed to keep across an update (scripts/lib.sh:setting, and the table in
# docs/RELEASING.md). Carries no secret, but it is machine-local BY DEFINITION:
# a tracked copy is exactly the thing an update would overwrite, which is what
# it exists to prevent. The committed template is demo-settings.env.example.
#
# Needs its own line -- `.env` above matches a file called exactly that, not
# this one.
.demo-settings.env

# Gateway logins, generated by scripts/make-env.sh from .secrets.env. Derived,
# never authored -- delete it and `make env` builds it again.
.gateways.env

# Local CA and TLS private keys, regenerated by the create-certs.sh scripts.
# The CA is machine-local on purpose: sharing it would mean sharing the ability
# to mint certificates every machine that trusts it would accept.
certs/
stacks/npm/certs/
# The leaf-only copy create-certs.sh writes for the SITE proxies. Same private
# key as certs/leaf.key, so it is just as gitignored.
stacks/npm/site-certs/

# Gateway backups contain the gateway's own credentials.
*.gwbk
*.sql
backup-*

# Third-party Ignition modules are licensed binaries, not our source.
# scripts/get-modules.sh fetches what is publishable and hash-checks the rest;
# see scripts/modules.manifest for where each one comes from.
modules/.cache/
# Needs the ** -- these live in per-gateway subfolders (modules/ignition/...),
# and `modules/*.modl` matches only the top level, which silently tracks ~96 MB
# of vendor binaries.
*.modl

# Which migrations have run on THIS machine (scripts/migrate.sh). Per-machine
# and derived -- the same reasoning as .update-applied below, and for the same
# hard reason: self-update refuses to run on a dirty tree, so a tracked file a
# timer rewrites would stop every update.
.migrations-applied
# What this machine HAD before an update: gateway backups and a config-resource
# export (scripts/snapshot.sh). A .gwbk carries the gateway's own credentials,
# and these are large. For inspection and manual restore only.
.snapshots/

# Working state -------------------------------------------------------------
# What scripts/update-check.sh last saw at origin. Per-machine and derived --
# and it MUST be ignored, because self-update.sh refuses to run on a dirty
# tree and a tracked file rewritten by a timer would make every update stop.
.update-state
# The commit self-update.sh last APPLIED to this machine's gateway -- which is
# not the same as the commit it last pulled, and is the difference between a
# repo that is current and a gateway that is.
.update-applied
# Which Ignition build each gateway's VOLUME has actually run, observed by
# scripts/ign-version.sh. Per-machine and about the volumes, not the repo --
# and it is what the downgrade guard falls back on once `make down` has
# removed the containers there was no other way to ask.
.ignition-version-seen
# The one part of the repo wd-control can WRITE -- it mounts everything else
# read-only. Holds the chosen Ignition version, which both the terminal and the
# demo console read, so the two cannot end up on different builds.
.wd-local/
_incoming/
.pull-backup/
project_mirror/

# Editor / OS ---------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~

.scratch/

# Gateway backups: gateway credentials, and large. scripts/gwbk.sh writes here.
.gwbk/
__pycache__/

# Playwright for scripts/e2e-demos.js. There is no package.json here on
# purpose -- the test is run from a checkout that already has playwright, by
# symlinking or pointing NODE_PATH at it. See docs/DEMO-CONSOLE.md.
node_modules

# Playwright MCP's own scratch output (console/page dumps). Written into the
# working directory by whatever drives a browser here, never a repo artefact.
.playwright-mcp/

# Claude Code writes per-machine permission choices here. Machine-local by
# definition, and an untracked file left lying about makes self-update.sh
# refuse to run -- its dirty-tree guard cannot tell yours from a real edit.
.claude/
.vscode/

# Screenshots from `make shot`. Verification output, not a repo artefact.
.shots/

# A command output captured with tee in the checkout must not block make update.
/*.log
